<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ladislaus IV of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1262">1262</a>–1290</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ladislaus the Cuman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ladislaus IV, called the Cuman after his mother's people, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1272 to 1290. Crowned as a child, he struggled with baronial factions throughout his reign. His cavalry helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">Rudolf of Habsburg</a> defeat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a> on the Marchfeld in 1278, and he repelled a second Mongol invasion in 1285–1286, but his favour to the pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> brought papal hostility. He was murdered in 1290.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Ladislaus IV of Hungary" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Szilágyi Sándor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ladislav4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
